<%# The shared <head> of the two layouts for the owner: admin and auth. Both load the same bundle,
    and no page here is public. That is the reason for the noindex on each one. %>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<title><%= [ title.presence, t("admin.site_name") ].compact.join(" · ") %></title>
<%# ⚠️ This is here, and public/ serves it, and not Propshaft. With no declaration, the browser
    keeps the last icon that it saw for this origin, which is the icon of Sidekiq, because
    Sidekiq::Web has one and the admin had none. An /assets path with a fingerprint would not
    correct a bookmark either: a bookmark makes a plain /favicon.ico request, and only public/
    answers that. %>
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32">
<%= csrf_meta_tags %>
<%# Turbo puts this nonce on each script that it adds, and it refreshes the tag at each visit. That
    is why each request can have its own nonce and a Drive navigation still works. %>
<%= csp_meta_tag %>

<script nonce="<%= content_security_policy_nonce %>">
  // The dark theme of Web Awesome uses a `.wa-dark` class, and not prefers-color-scheme. Thus this
  // code puts the setting of the operating system on that class. It is inline and it runs before
  // the paint, thus the light theme never appears first. Turbo replaces <body> and joins the two
  // <head> elements, but it never changes <html>. Thus the class stays through a Drive visit and
  // this code needs to run only at a full page load.
  // ⚠️ The nonce is what lets this run under the CSP in OwnerFacing. Do not remove it, and do not
  // move this code into the bundle: it must run before the paint.
  (function () {
    var query = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)");
    var apply = function (event) {
      document.documentElement.classList.toggle("wa-dark", event.matches);
    };
    apply(query);
    query.addEventListener("change", apply);
  })();
</script>

<%# ⚠️ Never change an attribute of a data-turbo-track element at run time. Turbo puts the outerHTML
    of that element into its signature, thus a change makes each navigation a full page load. %>
<%= stylesheet_link_tag "admin", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<%= javascript_include_tag "admin", defer: true, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
